      "why": "Full pipeline gives 1 result/cycle, so 32 results take 32 cycles. At Fmax ~200 MHz that is 160 ns, well under the 440 ns p99 batch bound. It is the cleanest way to meet the throughput and latency constraints simultaneously. I focus on the minimal data_width/n_iter that meets max_abs_err <= 2^-12 (0.000244141). For CORDIC, error ~ 2^-(n_iter+1) roughly, so n_iter=12-14 with W=14-16 should suffice. angle_guard and frac_guard kept low to minimize area. Rounding explored to see if it helps accuracy at lower n_iter."
